From: Andreas Baumann <mail@andreasbaumann.cc>
Subject: Fix FTBFS with GCC 15

GCC 15 defaults to the C23 standard, under which an empty parameter
list such as "void srand48();" or "unsigned sleep();" means a function
taking no arguments, rather than "unspecified arguments" as under
older C standards.  include/system.h declares srand48() and sleep()
this way, which now conflicts with the real prototypes in glibc's
stdlib.h/unistd.h and breaks the build.

Build with -std=gnu17 to keep the old "unspecified arguments"
semantics, matching the fix used by Debian bug #1096720.
---
 src/Makefile  | 2 +-
 util/Makefile | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/src/Makefile
+++ b/src/Makefile
@@ -159,7 +159,7 @@
 # flags for debugging:
 # CFLAGS = -g -I../include

-CFLAGS = -O -I../include
+CFLAGS = -O -I../include -std=gnu17
 LFLAGS = 

 # The Qt and Be window systems are written in C++, while the rest of
--- a/util/Makefile
+++ b/util/Makefile
@@ -94,7 +94,7 @@
 # flags for debugging:
 # CFLAGS = -g -I../include

-CFLAGS = -O -I../include
+CFLAGS = -O -I../include -std=gnu17
 LFLAGS =

 LIBS =
